# Shuri, Wakandan Inventor: "Artifact spells you cast cost {1} less to cast" and "{1}, {T}: Target artifact you control becomes a
# copy of a second target artifact you control until end of turn, except it isn't legendary. Activate only as a sorcery." Cast in
# turn 1 for {1}{U} (from a Black Lotus, which ends in the graveyard). In turn 3 Iron Lad ({2}{U}, an artifact creature) costs {1}{U}, paid exactly by those
# two Moxen (the pool is empty); A.I.M. Scientists ({3}{U}), not an artifact spell, gets no discount: with the Moxen's three mana ({U}{B}{W}) it is refused (Mana: short). Then Shuri taps with Mox
# Pearl's {W} for {1} and makes Bot1's Mox Pearl a copy of Iron Lad until end of turn: a 2/2 flying, vigilance artifact creature
# that is not legendary, so the legend rule leaves both. The same Mox is refused as the second target (CR 115.3), and Bot2's Mox Ruby and the Black Lotus card in Bot1's graveyard (not a permanent) as either target.

